eenwood has set <strong>126 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 125 that chance alone would give, and <strong>187 record highs</strong>, more than the 125 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (98). Greenwood's all-time high is 106\u00b0F, on August 30, 2000.","t_chg":"Greenwood's days got warmer. Its nights didn't.","p_chg":"Across 74 complete years: Greenwood's average low shows no clear change: +0.08\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.05 to +0.20) that includes zero. Greenwood's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.33\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.50), about +2.5\u00b0F since 1949.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none. Highs rose in 5 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Greenwood's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.26 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 51.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 1989 (79.97 in); the driest, 1965 (32.31 in). Greenwood almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.2 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 33 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}